<title>ITALY: Italy's Turin see July CPI at 0.0pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Turin see July CPI at 0.0pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Turin said its July consumer price index (CPI) stood at 0.0 percent month-on-month and 1.6 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In June, Turin's CPI inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 1.7 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Turin is one of 11 Italian cities to publish inflation data Monday and Tuesday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 8.81 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>The following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to June 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.0    (0.1)    1.6  (1.7)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.2    (0.1)   -0.9 (-0.4)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0    (0.2)    4.3  (4.3)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.4    (0.0)    6.2  (5.9)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0    (0.0)    1.2  (1.3)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0    (0.1)    2.0  (1.9)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.0    (0.1)    1.1  (1.3)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.1   (-0.2)   -1.1 (-1.0)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0    (0.0)    1.0  (1.0)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0    (0.1)    0.6  (0.7)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	-0.2    (0.2)    3.7  (4.1)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129507</p>
